    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d696">

                <pb facs="0648" n="564" sameAs="frus:frus1918Supp02/pg564"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 891.48/30</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Minister in Persia</hi>
                        (<hi rendition="#italic">Caldwell</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1918-01-10T18:00:00-05:00">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">January 10, 1918, 6 p.m.</hi>
                        </date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>23. Your December 10, 9 a.m. If American Red Cross undertakes to furnish relief
                    for famine how could relief supplies best be purchased and distributed?</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Lansing</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
